{# AO·09 · THE SCIENTIFIC RECORD, DEMOTED TO A WIDGET — and, in this app, ABSENT.

   The ruling was: demoted, never deleted. Forest loss and fire detections belong on this page as
   one card that is OFF by default, because an area manager's morning question is not what the
   canopy did in 2013 — but a design that quietly drops real data it once showed would be a design
   that lied about its priorities rather than restating them.

   THE HONEST PART: this app has no forest-loss and no fire-detection data. There is no Hansen/UMD
   series and no VIIRS ingestion behind it — no table, no endpoint. The charts that used to sit at
   the top of this page were drawn against a source that does not exist here, so redrawing them
   would be worse than demoting them. The card keeps its place in the catalogue, off by default,
   and says what it is waiting for.
   → the ingestion for both series is unbuilt. #}
